ironment/network/file inputs affecting build outputs with source and generator provenance. Negative fixture: Reject unrecorded nonhermetic influence or explicitly mark it according to the declared reproducibility policy; never silently certify hermeticity. Required evidence: build-input manifest and clean/replayed input-drift fixture; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime, schema outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.", :id "build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-typed-graph-under-declared-build-effects", :before "- [ ] `build/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/execute-typed-graph-under-declared-build-effects` Execute typed graph under declared build effects\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Build architecture](../../docs/phase-12-build-package-and-artifact-system/166-pkg2-build-system-architecture.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Clean build node receipts and undeclared environment/network/shell rejection. SAFE14 also denies undeclared postinstall, model/tool, compiler IR and unproven native generation/registry authority; permitted effects carry provider, scope, grant and trace, and hermetic release effects are replayable or have pinned outputs. Negative fixtures prove denial occurs before the external effect.", :after-sha256 "7f7878c64f70416f80053c1742dadda29314c4f2b4e35fab7dcc9542db263e8c"} {:path "specs/platform-workflow/tasks.md", :before-present? true, :criterion-ids ["acceptance/domain/device-adaptation" "acceptance/domain/device-uart-integration" "acceptance/domain/typed-mmio"], :before-sha256 "f36970d280aebd2fac7ced87d930045eb12110daec0db48d36b7a014ed6dcdad", :field-path [:canonical-task-record], :marker "platform-implementation-tasks", :preserved-status :open, :after "- [ ] `devices` Devices / `devices`\n\nStatus: Open\n\nDeclared completion and remaining work: Adopt device/provider interfaces; implement ownership-aware MMIO/interrupt/transfer adapters; validate denial without grants, lifetime handling and device failure translation. DOM4 acceptance requires register address/width/alignment/endian/volatile/order and audited-wrapper records, DMA ownership/lifetime/pinning/coherency/synchronization/completion, interrupt effects/cleanup and hosted/mobile permission/lifecycle/thread/null/error/taint contracts where applicable. Exercise UART transmit/receive/overflow/acknowledgement plus DMA lifetime and grant-denial cases; emit register/MMIO/DMA/interrupt/capability manifests and simulator/device evidence. Dependencies: profile legality, ownership, FFI and runtime device boundaries; vendor calls alone establish no safe behavior. Criterion `domain/device-adaptation`: Expose vendor/hosted/mobile device APIs through typed permission/lifecycle/thread/null/error/taint adapters. Accepted fixture: Invoke typed hosted/mobile/vendor device adapters with permission, lifecycle, thread/actor, null/error and taint contracts. Negative fixture: Reject missing permissions, lifecycle/thread violations, unchecked nulls or a vendor call presented as safe without a boundary. Required evidence: device adapter manifest and permission/lifecycle/error fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/device-uart-integration`: Execute the declared UART driver slice with register/DMA/interrupt evidence and denied unauthorized/unsafe accesses. Accepted fixture: Run UART transmit/receive/overflow/interrupt acknowledgement with register, DMA, lifetime and synchronization records. Negative fixture: Reject unauthorized MMIO, invalid DMA lifetime or interrupt cleanup/effect violations. Required evidence: register/MMIO/DMA manifests and simulator/device trace; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume runtime/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-memory-concurrency-and-typed-ffi-boundaries, auth/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/enforce-grant-intersection-attenuation-revocation-phase-and-lifetime outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/typed-mmio`: Perform register/MMIO access under explicit address/width/alignment/endian/volatile/ordering/authority and audited-wrapper contracts. Accepted fixture: Validate register address, width, alignment, endian, volatile and ordering behavior with explicit authority and unsafe/audited safe-wrapper contracts. Negative fixture: Reject untyped, nonvolatile, misaligned, unordered or ungranted MMIO access. Required evidence: register schema, MMIO audit and register-access fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume runtime/remaining-tasks-and