a7a72c4"} {:path "specs/platform-workflow/tasks.md", :before-present? true, :criterion-ids ["acceptance/domain/hardware-fifo-integration" "acceptance/domain/hardware-hdl-emission" "acceptance/domain/hardware-shape-lowering"], :before-sha256 "033a5967751d898f71dfa828ed7b56e3f6fa472df76fcc417bb5c58cff097834", :field-path [:canonical-task-record], :marker "platform-implementation-tasks", :preserved-status :open, :after "- [ ] `hardware` Hardware / `hardware`\n\nStatus: Open\n\nDeclared completion and remaining work: Adopt clock/reset/HDL target contract; implement state-machine lowering and simulation; verify timing/reset invariants and reject illegal dynamic/runtime operations; emit traceable hardware artifact. DOM1 acceptance requires fixed synthesis-visible shapes, finite iteration and explicit CDC synchronizer/FIFO/handshake, proof or audit waiver; reject implicit widths/truncation, unsafe CDC, runtime-only constructs and nonfinite loops. Emit HDL, interface/clock/reset/timing records, source maps, testbench and simulation evidence. Exercise FIFO full/empty/reset/backpressure/data order plus counter and bus-peripheral fixtures. Dependencies: profile legality, HDL lowering, no-runtime and safety/proof consumers; target choice remains open ; P8 target conformance requires fixed-width shape/overflow checks, static unroll or structural conversion or rejection, explicit input-only nondeterminism, state-graph emission AND validation (initial/reset/transition/output/illegal-state behavior), clock/reset records (explicit uninitialized state allowed; unsafe power-on needs hardware audit), ports/protocols and CDC synchronizer/FIFO/handshake/proof or audited waiver. Reject runtime services and unmediated CDC. Capability targets must validate bounds/provenance/permissions/sealing/derivation, tags across register/memory/DMA/FIFO/bus/debug/port paths, declared compartment entry/return/shared-state authority and explicit temporal assumptions. Tag-destroying paths are marked and diagnosed unless source explicitly expects destruction; audited authority boundaries retain their conditions. A conforming target may declare no temporal revocation; stronger source requirements then reject or require separate proof. Emit source-mapped hardware IR/HDL, target/layout/tag/clock/reset/timing/port/compartment reports and positive/negative capability-target fixtures. ISA/product/fabrication selection remains unassessed. Criterion `domain/hardware-fifo-integration`: Demonstrate the declared FIFO slice including full/empty/reset/backpressure/data-order behavior and absence of forbidden runtime services. Accepted fixture: Simulate the FIFO full, empty, reset, backpressure and data-order cases using fixed shapes, declared clocks and ready/valid interfaces. Negative fixture: Reject heap/host IO/dynamic dispatch, nonfinite control and missing CDC/timing evidence. Required evidence: HDL, testbench, interface/timing/source maps and simulation trace; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-hdl, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/hardware-hdl-emission`: Emit traceable HDL, interface/clock/reset/timing records and executable simulation/testbench artifacts for accepted hardware IR. Accepted fixture: Emit HDL and source maps from accepted hardware IR together with interface, clock/reset/timing and simulation/testbench artifacts. Negative fixture: Reject an artifact missing source maps, typed vendor-IP boundary, timing constraints or simulation/equivalence evidence. Required evidence: traceable HDL artifact pack and conformance report; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-hdl, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/hardware-shape-lowering`: Lower typed fixed-shape hardware values/control to finite hardware/domain IR, rejecting implicit widths/truncation and nonfinite runtime-only operations. Accepted fixture: Lower fixed-width/signed/shape signals, registers, ports, buses, memories and finite state/control under declared clock/reset/layout and truncation contracts. Negative fixture: Reject implicit host widths, undeclared truncation, software-pointer/runtime dependencies and control that cannot become finite hardware. Required evidence: finite hardware IR, shape/clock/reset records and rejected-source diagnostics; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-hdl, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-profile-restrictions-and-generated-form-checks outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.\n\nSource basis: [Hardware contract](../../docs/phase-09-domain-specific-computing-coverage/124-dom1-hardware-computing-domain-specification.md)", :id "hardware", :before "- [ ] `hardware` Hardware / `hardware`\n\nStatus: Open\n\nDeclared completion and remaining work: Adopt clock/reset/HDL target contract; implement state-machine lowering an