omponent completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed. Criterion `domain/kernel-user-boundary`: Enforce typed syscall/user-kernel input, taint, capability and error contracts with audited privileged implementation boundaries. Accepted fixture: Enforce declared syscall schemas, user-pointer validation/taint, capabilities and error translation through audited privileged wrappers. Negative fixture: Reject schema-less/taint-unsafe entry, unaudited raw memory and ambient authority. Required evidence: kernel ABI/syscall schema, wrapper audit and boundary fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-llvm, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/complete-ownership-borrow-initialization-and-lifetime-analysis outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.\n\nSource basis: [Kernel contract](../../docs/phase-09-domain-specific-computing-coverage/126-dom3-operating-system-and-kernel-domain-specification.md)", :id "kernel", :before "- [ ] `kernel` Kernel / `kernel`\n\nStatus: Open\n\nDeclared completion and remaining work: Adopt kernel ABI/execution model; implement initialization, memory and scheduling interface slice required by contract; verify unsafe boundaries, no hidden hosted services and artifact provenance. DOM3 acceptance requires typed syscall/user-pointer taint, capability and error mapping; raw-memory safe-wrapper/audit, allocation/panic/preemption/interrupt and ABI records. Exercise valid/invalid syscall, interrupt, allocator and page-table cases, reject ambient authority and hosted assumptions, and emit kernel object/boot image, syscall/interrupt tables, audit/capability/source maps and named emulator smoke evidence. Dependencies: profile legality, native lowering, ownership and runtime/FFI boundaries; OS product architecture remains unadopted ; P7 target conformance requires explicit page/frame/pinned/address-space/DMA and interrupt-safe allocator/failure/concurrency policy; reject hidden allocation/hosted services and unsupported atomics/fences. Check interrupt reentrancy/shared state/stack/latency/effects and scheduler block/sleep/preempt/allocate/context/lock rules; reject blocking in invalid lock or interrupt context. Driver ABI/device/grant/buffer/DMA/callback/error/unsafe-wrapper records retain provenance; actual device transfer and callback entry are separate Runtime/Devices consumers. Emit capability/memory/device/interrupt/scheduler/atomic/ABI/unsafe/no-hidden-allocation evidence. OS architecture/product selection remains unassessed\n\nSource basis: [Kernel contract](../../docs/phase-09-domain-specific-computing-coverage/126-dom3-operating-system-and-kernel-domain-specification.md)", :after-sha256 "19db9033d372ab01bfa7a847fed4a79d42753304fb5efa0ea2510bf8578a5658"} {:path "specs/legality-workflow/tasks.md", :before-present? true, :criterion-ids ["acceptance/runtime/check-proof-preservation"], :before-sha256 "29422030427094705642da7d0117f3801f52af6c174c8e24117531c5cc7a0001", :field-path [:canonical-task-record], :marker "legality-implementation-tasks", :preserved-status :open, :after "- [ ] `legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/preserve-obligations-into-mir-and-runtime-execution` Preserve obligations into MIR and runtime execution\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Safety pipeline](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/c10_safety_analysis/pipeline.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Surviving check/proof/source edges; missing-check and unjustified-elision rejection. For SAFE1/SAFE2/SAFE8/SAFE9/SAFE15, invalidate or regenerate affected facts after source, expansion, type/effect, profile/target, numeric mode, memory/capability provider, pass/backend, dependency, grant or replay changes. Verify imported certificate schema, exact inputs, compatibility and trust before use. Erase only the exact proved condition with surviving backend assumptions and recorded check/proof identities; restore the check or reject on invalidation. Manual review alone is insufficient unless governing claim policy explicitly permits it; authority, audit, replay and human-review gates retain their separate policy obligations. Criterion `runtime/check-proof-preservation`: Retain required bounds/numeric/initialization/alias/resource checks or applicable proof/trap/rejection evidence, including source/check identity and elision provenance. Accepted fixture: Preserve source/check identity and valid bounds/numeric/initialization/alias/resource proofs across lowering and runtime/target service boundaries. Negative fixture: On invalidation regenerate proof, retain the required check/trap or reject; reject proofless elision or lost policy evidence. Required evidence: check/proof/elision provenance and invalidation/rejection fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume mir/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/mir2-attach-fact-tables, lower/current-evidence-and-remaining-work/lower4-preserve-proofs-and-origins outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.", :id "legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/preserve-obligations-into-mir-and-runtime-execution", :before "- [ ] `legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/preserve-obligations-into-mir-and-runtime-execution` Preserve obligations into MIR and runtime execution\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Safety pipeline](../../bootstrap/clojure/src/gravity/c10_safety_analysis/pipeline.clj)\n\nClosing evidence: Surviving check/proof/source edges; missing-check and unjustified-elision rejection. For SAFE1/SAFE2/SAFE8/SAFE9/SAFE15, invalidate or regenerate affected facts after source, expansion, type/effect, profile/target, numeric mode, memory/capability provider, pass/backend, dependency, grant or replay changes. Verify imported certificate schema, exact inputs, compatibility and trust before use. Erase only the exact proved condition with surviving backend assumptions and recorded check/proof identities; restore the check or reject on invalidation. Manual review alone is insufficient unless governing claim policy explicitly permits it; authority, audit, replay and human-review gates retain their separate policy obligations.", :after-sha256 "56c27f96059fa03732ce648f37abf3073b6c5fc525998e58a8dfd6d850871966"} {:path "specs/domains-workflow/tasks.md", :before-present? true, :criterion-ids ["acceptance/domain/numeric-provider-binding" "acceptance/domain/scientific-sine-integration"], :before-sha256 "1179cebf48223c9403f5457e24f3d2dc655ffecc99744f9fa11c19523323a184", :field-path [:canonical-task-record], :marker "domains-implementation-tasks", :preserved-status :open, :after "- [ ] `math` Math\n\nStatus: Open\n\nProjected task block:\nOutcome: [math contracts](../../docs/phase-05-mathematical-and-elementary-function-system/README.md) execute with the declared\nnumeric semantics and checked justification for transformations. Remaining\nfinite tasks, all open: implement numeric-mode/domain checking; implement EFIR\nlowering and evaluation; connect EML/certificate checking to justified rewrites;\nimplement certified approximation/interval and symbolic operations; run the\ncontract conformance matrix with rejected unproved transformations.\n\nYes/no acceptance: do domain and branch errors reject? Do proof-dependent\nrewrites require checked evidence? Do strict-mode results match the selected\nsemantics? Integration: Types/MIR to EFIR, Opt proof preservation, Lower/Stdlib\nnumeric APIs. Decision owner: numeric maintainer; recommendation: keep EML as\nadjacent proof/search representation, never ordinary runtime equality authority.\n\nSAFE9 acceptance: execute checked/panic/wrapping/saturating/arbitrary-precision/proof-required integer modes, exceptional divisor/shift/minimum-negation cases and explicit float conversion behavior; reject implicit narrowing, hidden target defaults and unapproved relaxed math. Inspect strict/relaxed floating contracts including NaN, infinity, signed zero, rounding and fusion; elementary providers expose domain/range/accuracy/target evidence. Invalidated numeric proofs restore checks or reprove; target instructions preserve mode or are guarded/rejected. Explicit wrapping/saturating narrowing retains the source conflict with checked/proven narrowing until adjudicated. P2/P12 profile interface: check portable/core and exact/symbolic/interval/bitvector/rounded/certified mode eligibility and explicit conversions/assumptions; reject hidden target-default or provider-dependent core math. Formal symbolic lowering emits symbolic IR, theorem/assumption/trusted-kernel records and checked conclusions; imported proof validation and actual arithmetic remain distinct interfaces. Dependencies consume Types/Legality facts and declared proof-provider outputs, not completion of another component.\n\nCriterion `domain/numeric-provider-binding`: Bind external numeric libraries/providers to typed FFI, numeric-mode/domain/error and approximation contracts. Accepted fixture: Bind numeric providers with implementation/version, typed FFI, numeric mode/domain/range/error and approximation contracts. Negative fixture: Reject mode mismatches, unsafe/opaque FFI and provider-dependent results presented as portable semantics. Required evidence: numeric provider/FFI manifests and mode/reference boundary fixtures; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-llvm, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/preserve-obligations-into-mir-and-runtime-execution outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.\n\nCriterion `domain/scientific-sine-integration`: Demonstrate declared certified sine with EFIR/EML semantic evidence, exact numeric mode/domain/error guarantees and reproducible reference accuracy/performance. Accepted fixture: Emit certified sine for the declared domain/error contract using EFIR semantics, EML proof/search and checked approximation/roundoff/branch/target evidence. Negative fixture: Reject domain gaps, unverified certificate or unauthorized backend fast-math flags. Required evidence: EFIR/EML/certificate, native/GPU kernel and reference accuracy report; bind source/compiler/profile/target/provider identities, source-mapped stable diagnostics and every applicable source facet field/exception/negative condition listed for this criterion in specs/requirement-reconciliation/domain-gap-completion.edn. Dependencies consume backend-llvm, legality/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/preserve-obligations-into-mir-and-runtime-execution outputs under their stated contracts; no whole-component completion prerequisite. Status: Open; implementation acceptance unassessed.", :id "math", :before "- [ ] `math` Math\n\nStatus: Open\n\nProjected task block:\nOutcome: [math contracts](../../docs/phase-05-mathematical-and-elementary-function-system/README.md) execute with the declared\nnumeric semantics and checked justification for transformations. Remaining\nfinite tasks, all open: implement numeric-mode/domain checking; implement EFIR\nlowering and evaluation; connect EML/certificate checking to justified rewrites;\nimplement certified approximation/interval and symbolic operations; run the\ncontract conformance matrix with rejected unproved transformations.\n\nYes/no acceptance: do domain and branch errors reject? Do proof-dependent\nrewrites require checked evidence? Do strict-mode results match the selected\nsemantics? Integration: Types/MIR to EFIR, Opt proof preservation, Lower/Stdlib\nnumeric APIs. Decision owner: numeric maintainer; recommendation: keep EML as\nadjacent proof/search representation, never ordinary runtime equality authority.\n\nSAFE9 acceptance: execute checked/panic/wrapping/saturating/arbitrary-precision/proof-required integer modes, exceptional divisor/shift/minimum-negation cases and explicit float conversion behavior; reject implicit narrowing, hidden target defaults and unapproved relaxed math. Inspect strict/relaxed floating contracts including NaN, infinity, signed zero, rounding and fusion; elementary providers expose domain/range/accuracy/target evidence. Invalidated numeric proofs restore checks or reprove; target instructions preserve mode or are guarded/rejected. Explicit wrapping/saturating narrowing retains the source conflict with checked/proven narrowing until adjudicated. P2/P12 profile interface: check portable/core and exact/symbolic/interval/bitvector/rounded/certified mode eligibility and explicit conversions/assumptions; reject hidden target-default or provider-dependent core math. Formal symbolic lowering emits symbolic IR, theorem/assumption/trusted-kernel records and checked conclusions; imported proof validation and actual arithmetic remain distinct interfaces. Dependencies consume Types/Legality facts and declared proof-provider outputs, not completion of another component.", :after-sha256 "70c38a336681098bd5cbe821b33c6930a74575f189f7556da634dfae3495310c"} {:path "specs/compiler-api-workflow/tasks.md", :before-present? true, :criterion-ids ["acceptance/domain/mir-pass-integration"], :before-sha256 "9de4f866e91973223f0aac28e8d0db814884996855ce5d80761a7ef79d7ca1fe", :field-path [:canonical-task-record], :marker "compiler-api-implementation-tasks", :preserved-status :open, :after "- [ ] `pass-evidence` Pass Evidence: finite remaining tasks\n\nStatus: Open\n\nProjected task block:\nOwner role: compiler verification maintainer. All tasks open.\n\n| Task | Concrete closing evidence |\n| --- | --- |\n| Classify real pass population | Enumerate every pass in the declared compiler closure with version, risk, affected profiles/targets and governing minimum evidence; reject omitted passes or incompatible evidence classes. |\n| Execute required verification gates | Invoke actual schema/semantic verifiers at required compiler boundaries; bind reports to input/output identity and stop affected artifact production on failure rather than accepting supplied success flags. |\n| Bind transformation evidence | Changed MIR functions receive the governing translation validation or checked proof evidence; check-elision proofs/certificates are checked, and target lowering has actual differential/backend conformance receipts for claimed targets. |\n| Capture failures and preserve trust boundaries | Record counterexample input/output/property/diagnostic and source identities, retain the prior valid artifact after rejected transformation, and turn reproducible failures into regression fixtures. |\n| Emit truthful trust and release-gate records | Reports enumerate supported profiles/targets, residual evidence gaps and experimental gates; missing/high-risk/stale evidence blocks affected release artifacts. Release consumes this decision but independently owns final acceptance. |\n\nYes/no acceptance: do reports derive from actual checks on exact artifacts?\nAre plugin and backend passes included when used? Are absent evidence and\ncounterexamples visible? Do failures block the affected claimed release path?\nAll must be yes. No claim of a fully mechanized compiler is implied.\n\nCriterion `domain/mir-pass-integration`: Demonstrate the declared typed MIR pass with before/after semantic/provenance and rejected missing-